    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::timeline_namespace_collision": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::timeline_namespace_collision",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Two different `timeline` modules (astrid.timeline schema vs astrid.core.timeline CRUD) coexist with the same short name",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/timeline.py",
          "astrid/core/timeline/__init__.py",
          "astrid/core/timeline/crud.py",
          "astrid/core/task/lifecycle.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/schema.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/timeline.py is a 1,377-LOC module of TypedDict schemas (TimelineEffect, ParameterDefinition, ClipTransition, Pool, ArrangementVisualSource, \u2026) re-exported partly from banodoco_timeline_schema.",
          "astrid/core/timeline/ is a separate package providing CRUD operations (create_timeline, list_timelines, finalize_output, tombstone_timeline, \u2026) plus paths/defaults/migration/integrity submodules.",
          "Files such as astrid/core/task/lifecycle.py:73-74 import `from astrid.core.timeline.defaults import \u2026` and `from astrid.core.timeline.paths import \u2026`, while astrid/core/executor/schema.py:23 imports `from astrid.timeline import ClipClassifiedKind` \u2014 a developer scanning imports has to remember which `timeline` is which.",
          "There is no shared boundary or facade making the relationship between the two explicit; the schema module lives at the top level next to pipeline.py while the CRUD package is buried inside core/."
        ],
