    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::vendored_upstream_inside_pack": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::vendored_upstream_inside_pack",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "ostris/ai-toolkit submodule lives inside astrid/packs/seinfeld/ai_toolkit/upstream, blurring project vs vendor boundary",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          ".gitmodules",
          "astrid/packs/seinfeld/ai_toolkit/upstream",
          "astrid/packs/seinfeld/aitoolkit_stage/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/seinfeld/aitoolkit_train"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          ".gitmodules registers `astrid/packs/seinfeld/ai_toolkit/upstream` -> https://github.com/ostris/ai-toolkit.git, so the entire subtree (UI app, cron, hundreds of TS/TSX files, run.py, etc.) is a third-party vendor.",
          "Because the submodule sits under astrid/packs/, it is indistinguishable from project packs to anything that walks the packs root (registry.discover_packs, lint/test/scan tools). The package_size_census in the blind packet attributes 99.6% of LOC to `astrid` because of this submodule, distorting the size picture.",
          "Authoring norms inside the submodule (TypeScript Next.js UI with class-based React, prisma, console.error patterns) are alien to the rest of the codebase, but tooling treats them as first-party.",
          "There is no obvious boundary marker (e.g. a `vendor/` top-level directory or a registry exclusion) signalling that contributors should not edit code under upstream/."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move the submodule out of astrid/packs/ to a top-level `vendor/ai-toolkit/` directory and have astrid/packs/seinfeld/ai_toolkit/ refer to it via a thin path-based shim (or symlink only the entry points actually consumed by aitoolkit_stage/aitoolkit_train). Add an explicit exclusion list to scan/lint configs and to registry.discover_packs so that vendor code is never walked as if it were a pack. This removes the ambient confusion that the vendor tree IS the project, and lets future packs that wrap third-party code follow the same pattern.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "eb33f167"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:08:47+00:00",
