    "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::pack_layout_three_mental_models": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::pack_layout_three_mental_models",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Built-in packs use flat <pack>/<slug>/ but `packs new` + `executors new` + docs scaffold <pack>/executors/<slug>/, and structure.py only validates the flat shape.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "high_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/packs/cli.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/cli.py",
          "astrid/core/pack.py",
          "astrid/structure.py",
          "astrid/packs/validate.py",
          "docs/creating-packs.md"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Built-in shape: `astrid/packs/builtin/transcribe/{executor.yaml,run.py,STAGE.md}` \u2014 executor folder is a direct child of the pack.",
          "Scaffolder shape: astrid/packs/cli.py:219-221 creates `for subdir in ('executors','orchestrators','elements'): (target/subdir).mkdir()`. astrid/core/executor/cli.py:206-210 picks `content.get('executors', 'executors')` and writes to `<pack>/executors/<slug>/`.",
          "docs/creating-packs.md shows the canonical layout as `my_video_tools/executors/transcribe/executor.yaml` etc.",
          "astrid/structure.py:_validate_pack_executor_folders walks `_public_child_dirs(pack_dir)` directly \u2014 a scaffolded pack with executor.yaml under `<pack>/executors/<slug>/` would silently pass without ever being validated, because the validator never descends into the `executors/` subdirectory.",
          "Runtime registry side reconciles via astrid/core/pack.py:_content_roots() using `root.rglob(manifest_name)`, so both layouts load \u2014 masking the disagreement."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pick one canonical pack layout and converge on it. Recommended: keep the flat layout that the entire built-in fleet already uses, then (a) update astrid/packs/cli.py:_cmd_new and astrid/core/executor/cli.py:_scaffold_component to scaffold flat (drop the `executors/` and `orchestrators/` subdirs and the `content:` block in pack.yaml stub), (b) rewrite docs/creating-packs.md \u00a7'Repository Shape' to show the flat layout, and (c) extend structure.py to also walk one level into `executors/` and `orchestrators/` so legacy nested layouts remain validated. Alternatively, commit to nested and migrate the built-in packs \u2014 but that is a much larger move.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "b9ea26ca"
