          "'ai_toolkit' has no general meaning in the framework; it exists solely because astrid/packs/seinfeld/ai_toolkit/upstream/ is the ostris/ai-toolkit submodule that contains hundreds of nested files (Next.js app, Python jobs) that would otherwise be rglob'd as content roots.",
          "Result: framework code knows about a specific pack's vendored upstream \u2014 the inverse of pack-as-self-contained-bundle."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move the exclusion mechanism off-framework and onto the pack manifest. Add an optional `discovery: { exclude: [<glob>...] }` (or `content.exclude`) field to pack.yaml; have _content_roots read it from the PackDefinition.metadata. Then set `exclude: ['ai_toolkit/upstream/**']` in astrid/packs/seinfeld/pack.yaml and drop the hardcoded 'ai_toolkit' from core/pack.py. Framework stays generic; the seinfeld pack owns its own quirk.",
