    "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::model_trends_inline_iife_re_search": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::model_trends_inline_iife_re_search",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "ModelTrends recomputes a linear-interp lookup inline as an IIFE that duplicates the existing `cumulativeAt` helper",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "low_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/model-trends/component.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines ~535-551: `const cumulativeNow = (() => { ... linear search for bracketing series points ... })();` re-implements the same bracketing+lerp scan that `cumulativeAt` (lines 380-397) already encodes \u2014 only the input changes from a month string to a `targetT` time.",
          "An adjacent IIFE for `interpolatedHead` (lines 505-513) similarly hides a small named computation behind an anonymous expression."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Add `lerpSeriesAt(series, targetT)` (parameterized over time) and call `lerpSeriesAt(CUMULATIVE_MESSAGES, t0 + (t1 - t0) * chartProgress)` for `cumulativeNow` while `cumulativeAt` becomes a one-line wrapper that converts month string to time. Replace the `interpolatedHead` IIFE with a named local `interpolateRow(a, b, t)` function above the component. State and intent become explicit; no new module needed.",
