    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::executor_orchestrator_parallel_subsystems": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::executor_orchestrator_parallel_subsystems",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "executor and orchestrator subsystems duplicate seam logic across runner/registry/folder/api/cli with diverging behavior",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/executor/runner.py",
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/runner.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/folder.py",
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/folder.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/api.py",
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/api.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/registry.py",
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/registry.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/cli.py",
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/cli.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Both runners implement essentially the same flow: gate check \u2192 load registry \u2192 _prepare_project_request \u2192 thread_wrapper.begin_* \u2192 try _run_inner / finalize_exception / finalize_result \u2192 _finalize_project_* \u2192 status normalization. Code is 80%+ structurally identical with subtle drift (e.g. executor has check_binaries, orchestrator has python and command runtime branches; orchestrator returns OrchestratorPlan, executor does not).",
          "Both folder loaders run the same subprocess extraction pattern with a hand-written _EXTRACT_SCRIPT, _RESULT_PREFIX sentinel, and _attach_folder_metadata; the script bodies differ only by terminology (EXECUTOR/ORCHESTRATOR) and validate function. Same applies to OrchestratorSpec/ExecutorSpec, _to_plain, _drop_blank_defaults in api.py.",
          "Diff of orchestrator/cli.py vs executor/cli.py shows shared subparser shape with subtle divergences \u2014 the run subcommand passthrough handling (`_split_run_passthrough`) exists only on the orchestrator side, while --check-binaries and --timeline-id exist only on the executor side."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce a shared `astrid/core/runnable` (or similar) module that owns: (1) the project-run + thread-wrapper + gate harness used by both runners; (2) the placeholder expansion + _expand_placeholders + missing-placeholder error; (3) the folder extractor subprocess scaffold parameterized by sentinel/Spec/Definition; (4) the Spec\u2192Definition normalizer (_to_plain / _drop_blank_defaults). Have ExecutorRunner and OrchestratorRunner compose this seam rather than each maintaining their own copy. Even keeping two runner classes is fine \u2014 the seam helpers should live in one place.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "f3b3f0ff"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:08:47+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-15T23:08:47+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-05-16T00:14:36+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
