      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "core/executor/runner.py imports specific packs and branches on executor id at the dispatch seam",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/executor/runner.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/hype.py",
          "astrid/packs/upload/youtube/src/social_publish.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 39-51: `_pipeline_module()` lazy-imports `astrid.packs.builtin.hype` and `_builtin_steps_by_name()` is called from _run_builtin_executor and build_executor_command \u2014 core executor runtime is wired to one specific pack, contradicting the executor-as-plugin model the rest of the registry assumes.",
          "Lines 130-183: `_run_executor_inner` short-circuits on `executor.id == 'upload.youtube'` and `_run_upload_youtube` then `from astrid.packs.upload.youtube.src.social_publish import publish_youtube_video` \u2014 a hard boundary conditional in the dispatch path, plus another core\u2192pack import.",
          "Same module also imports from `astrid.packs.builtin.hype` inside `_optional_asset_path` and `_parse_asset_pairs` (`pipeline.asset_cache.is_url(...)`) for the URL check, which leaks asset-cache knowledge into the runner."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make the runner protocol-driven: the executor runtime kind should not need to know about specific packs. Either (a) lift the youtube path to a normal external executor invoked the same way every other executor is, or (b) give the executor schema a `runtime: 'python_callable'` kind whose target is declared in the manifest, then upload.youtube and the hype pipeline-step shim become regular registrations rather than special branches in core. Move the `is_url` check to a shared utility (e.g. astrid/utilities) instead of importing it from a pack.",
