    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::orchestrator_registry_silently_ignores_banodoco_config": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::orchestrator_registry_silently_ignores_banodoco_config",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "OrchestratorRegistry.load_default_registry accepts banodoco_config but never uses it, while the CLI builds and passes one",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/registry.py",
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/cli.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "registry.py line 132: `def load_default_registry(*, executor_registry=None, banodoco_config: Any | None = None) -> OrchestratorRegistry:` \u2014 banodoco_config is the parameter name and `Any | None` is the type, but `grep banodoco_config registry.py` shows it appears only in the signature; the body neither reads it nor delegates anywhere that does.",
          "cli.py line 35: `registry = load_default_registry(banodoco_config=_banodoco_config_from_args(args))`, where `_banodoco_config_from_args` (line 157+) constructs a fully-formed `BanodocoCatalogConfig` from CLI flags and env. The seam is wired on the call side and dropped on the receiver side, so `--banodoco-agent-orchestrators`, `--banodoco-catalog-url`, etc., are silently no-ops."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either (a) implement Banodoco catalog loading in the orchestrator registry the same way `load_pack_executors` + `load_banodoco_catalog_executors` is composed in the executor registry, then call it when `banodoco_config.enabled`; or (b) remove the parameter and the CLI flags entirely with a clear error if a user passes them. Do not leave a typed parameter that does nothing.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "7894d9c3"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
