    "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::runpod_mixed_sync_async": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::runpod_mixed_sync_async",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "astrid.core.runpod exposes async storage helpers next to sync sweep(), forcing every caller to bridge with asyncio.run().",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/runpod/storage.py",
          "astrid/core/runpod/sweeper.py",
          "astrid/pipeline.py",
          "astrid/packs/external/runpod/run.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "storage.py:10 `async def ensure_storage(...)` and storage.py:55 `async def list_volumes(...)` are public async APIs.",
          "sweeper.py:110 `def sweep(...)` is sync and internally calls `asyncio.run(_sweep_async(...))` (line 134).",
          "Callers re-implement the sync bridge ad-hoc: pipeline.py:540 `asyncio.run(_volumes_ls())`, pipeline.py:574 `asyncio.run(_ensure())`, packs/external/runpod/run.py:191/294/596 each wrap an inline `async def` in `asyncio.run(...)`.",
          "Two sibling modules in one package present opposite calling conventions for the same RunPod domain."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pick one posture for the runpod public surface. Either make sweep() async (consistent with storage), or add sync `ensure_storage_sync` / `list_volumes_sync` wrappers in storage.py and have callers stop hand-rolling `asyncio.run` blocks. Document which functions are awaitable in the package __init__.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "fd79bc84"
