          "astrid/core/worker/banodoco_worker.py:132-168 documents and enforces FLAG-013: 'JWKS verification proves identity, not project ownership' \u2014 the worker reads projects.user_id via service-role and gates the write on a match before invoking save_timeline.",
          "astrid/core/project/cli.py:367-371 (`if args.service_role: write_auth = ('service_role', reigh_env.resolve_service_role_key())`) wires the same service-role key straight into provider.save_timeline with no project-ownership read.",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/open_in_reigh/run.py:182-185 follows the same pattern \u2014 `--service-role` swaps the auth tuple to service_role and calls provider.save_timeline without a prior ownership check.",
          "Help text on both flags labels them 'Worker-only escape hatch' / 'Avoid for ownership-bound CLI calls', i.e. the inconsistency is acknowledged but not enforced in code."
