        ],
        "evidence": [
          "model-trends/component.tsx line 419-425 declares `props: { clip: any; params: any; theme: unknown; fps: number; assetEntry?: ... }` then line 428-429 re-binds `const clip: any = props.clip; const params: ChartParams = (clip.params ?? props.params ?? {}) as ChartParams;` \u2014 the same payload is read from two prop slots and cast back to a typed shape, with neither path documented as the canonical contract.",
          "html_canvas_effect/templates/card/component.tsx line 67-72 mixes `clip: any` with `params: unknown; theme: unknown` in the same prop bag without rationale, then casts `(props.params ?? {}) as EffectParams` immediately.",
          "Both Anchor- and ChartParams-typed shapes already exist in these files, so the `any` on the public clip/params surface is a typing-deferral, not a true contract gap."
