    "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::scaffold_layout_mismatch": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::scaffold_layout_mismatch",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Three uncoordinated pack layouts: scaffold creates <pack>/executors/<slug>/, validator walks the same nested path, structure.py only accepts flat <pack>/<slug>/ \u2014 and built-in packs use the flat shape, so validate_pack silently skips component checks for builtin.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "high_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/packs/cli.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/cli.py",
          "astrid/packs/validate.py",
          "astrid/structure.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/cut/executor.yaml",
          "docs/creating-packs.md"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/packs/cli.py:219-232 creates `executors/`, `orchestrators/`, `elements/` subdirectories under the pack root and reports them as the canonical layout.",
          "astrid/core/executor/cli.py:206-210 defaults `rel_dir = content.get(f'{component_type}s', f'{component_type}s')` so `executors new builtin.foo` lands at astrid/packs/builtin/executors/foo/, not astrid/packs/builtin/foo/.",
          "astrid/packs/validate.py:351-369 only walks pack_root/'executors' (etc.) when that directory exists, so the in-tree built-in pack (no executors/ subdir) silently passes component validation.",
          "astrid/structure.py:104-125 _validate_pack_executor_folders calls _public_child_dirs(pack_dir) once and looks for executor.yaml directly in each child \u2014 the flat layout. It would NOT find executors created by the scaffold.",
          "All ~48 in-tree executor.yaml files live one level under their pack (the flat shape), so the codebase as it ships has voted with its feet for flat \u2014 but the scaffold and validator still teach nested."
        ],
