        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/cli.py:335-353 and astrid/core/executor/cli.py:652-669 are two byte-similar copies of the same helper.",
          "Both wrap the entire ThreadIndexStore read (including the import) in `except Exception:` and print 'active_thread: unavailable' \u2014 a regression in ThreadIndexStore (e.g. schema drift, pickle/json corruption, import error from a moved module) is indistinguishable from 'no thread index file exists'.",
          "Two copies means a fix in one will silently regress the other \u2014 the canonical narrowing must happen twice or be missed."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move _print_active_thread_footer into astrid/threads/index.py (or astrid/threads/cli_helpers.py) as a single shared helper, and inside it narrow the catch to the actually-expected failure modes \u2014 `(FileNotFoundError, json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError)` \u2014 and emit a one-line stderr like `active_thread: unavailable ({exc.__class__.__name__}: {exc})` so a real ThreadIndexStore regression shows up instead of vanishing into the same string as 'no index file yet'.",
