      "id": "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::codemod_global_regex_test_with_lastindex_reset",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Codemod uses global regex .test() + manual SOURCE_REGEX.lastIndex = 0 reset for boolean probes",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "low_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "scripts/codemod-theme-api-imports.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "SOURCE_REGEX is declared with the /g flag at line 69 (needed for replaceAll-style iteration in findImports).",
          "Lines 258-259 and 289-292 then use it for boolean checks via `.test()` and immediately reset `SOURCE_REGEX.lastIndex = 0` to prevent the next call from skipping forward.",
          "This is a well-known JS footgun \u2014 any future caller that forgets the reset will see intermittent false negatives on the second invocation."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Declare a separate non-global probe regex (e.g. `const SOURCE_PROBE = new RegExp(SOURCE_REGEX.source);` without the /g flag) and call `SOURCE_PROBE.test(text)` for boolean checks; keep SOURCE_REGEX for the iteration path. Deletes both lastIndex reset lines.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "a7d42093"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
