      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Repeated `src={spriteUrl as string}` casts inside truthy-narrowed branches indicate lost flow narrowing \u2014 either the narrowing should be hoisted or the type widened honestly",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/text-card/component.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 329-331: `const spriteUrl = props.assetEntry?.file ?? props.assetEntry?.url; const isVideo = !!spriteUrl && /.../.test(spriteUrl); const isImage = !!spriteUrl && /.../.test(spriteUrl);` \u2014 `spriteUrl` is `string | undefined`.",
          "Lines 369, 380, 478: inside `if (isVideo)` / `if (isImage)` / similar branches, the JSX still writes `src={spriteUrl as string}` and `src={ctaUrl as string}` rather than relying on flow narrowing.",
          "Because the narrowing flag (`isVideo`/`isImage`) is a separate boolean from the variable, TypeScript cannot infer that `spriteUrl` is `string` inside those branches; the cast is the symptom."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace the boolean flags with an early-return narrowing: `if (!spriteUrl) return <fallback />;` (or hoist the sprite block into a child component that takes `spriteUrl: string`). Then `isVideo`/`isImage` are computed against a `string` and the `as string` casts go away.",
