        "evidence": [
          "astrid/packs/builtin/generate_image/run.py:53 `def _die(message: str) -> None:` body is `print(...); raise SystemExit(1)`",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/hype/run.py:86 `def usage_error(message: str) -> None:` body is `print(message, file=sys.stderr); raise SystemExit(2)`",
          "Same pattern in video_understand/run.py:66, visual_understand/run.py:39, tile_video/run.py:15, audio_understand/run.py:58, boundary_candidates/run.py:15 \u2014 all declare `-> None` but unconditionally raise SystemExit"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Change the annotation to `-> NoReturn` (import `from typing import NoReturn`). This is a single-line fix per file and lets type checkers correctly narrow types after a _die / usage_error call (e.g. eliminate the false Optional[int] in sprite_sheet._read_rgba_png).",
