      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "remotion/package.json pairs react@^18.3.1 runtime with @types/react@^19.2.14 (and @types/react-dom@^19.2.3) \u2014 types one major ahead of runtime.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "dependency_health",
        "related_files": [
          "remotion/package.json"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "remotion/package.json declares `\"react\": \"^18.3.1\"` (line 20) but `\"@types/react\": \"^19.2.14\"` and `\"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.2.3\"` (lines 27-28). React 18 and React 19 differ in JSX/ReactElement/ReactNode definitions; typing with the wrong major silently misreports component prop and children types in any tsc --noEmit run.",
          "remotion/src/Root.tsx imports `type {ReactElement} from 'react'` \u2014 exactly the typing surface that drifts between major versions.",
          "package-lock.json shows the same react@^18.3.1 vs @types/react@^19.2.14 pinning, so the mismatch is real on disk, not just a manifest typo."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pin @types/react and @types/react-dom to a `^18.x` line that matches the React 18 runtime (e.g. `@types/react@^18.3.x`, `@types/react-dom@^18.3.x`). If the intent is to upgrade to React 19, bump the runtime instead and verify Remotion 4.0.455's React 19 support before doing so.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "bdc2ba46"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
