      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "runpod_lifecycle / banodoco_timeline_schema / banodoco_social / banodoco_worker are imported but absent from requirements.txt with no install instructions in README.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "dependency_health",
        "related_files": [
          "requirements.txt",
          "astrid/core/runpod/storage.py",
          "astrid/core/runpod/sweeper.py",
          "astrid/packs/external/runpod/run.py",
          "astrid/timeline.py",
          "astrid/packs/upload/youtube/src/social_publish.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/core/runpod/storage.py:40 and :66 do bare `from runpod_lifecycle import Pod` / `from runpod_lifecycle import api` inside async functions \u2014 no try/except, no install hint. Same pattern in astrid/core/runpod/sweeper.py and many call sites of astrid/packs/external/runpod/run.py.",
          "astrid/timeline.py:24-35 imports banodoco_timeline_schema inside a try/except ImportError with TypedDict fallbacks, so timeline.py degrades gracefully, but the failure mode is silent: callers may see different runtime types depending on whether the sibling package is installed.",
          "astrid/packs/upload/youtube/src/social_publish.py imports banodoco_social.youtube / banodoco_social.models inside a function (lines noted in grep) \u2014 no docs on where this package lives or how to install it.",
          "requirements.txt and README.md contain zero mention of runpod_lifecycle, banodoco_timeline_schema, banodoco_social, or banodoco_worker. A fresh checkout cannot satisfy these imports from the declared manifest alone."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either (a) add the sibling repos as editable installs in requirements-dev.txt / a pyproject extras_require with a path or git URL, or (b) document the expected sibling-repo layout in README.md (the .gitmodules pattern already used for ai-toolkit is a reasonable template). For storage.py and sweeper.py specifically, wrap the imports in a try/except that raises a single clear 'install runpod_lifecycle from <repo>' error so the missing-dep failure surfaces once instead of as random AttributeErrors deep in async paths.",
