        "evidence": [
          "Lines 67-75: `export default function HtmlCanvasEffect(props: { clip: any; params: unknown; theme: unknown; fps: number; }): ReactElement { ... const params = (props.params ?? {}) as EffectParams; }` \u2014 bypasses the documented ElementComponentProps contract and uses both an `any` field (clip) and an unchecked `as` cast for params.",
          "Sibling effect components astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/text-card/component.tsx (lines 145-152) and astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/model-trends/component.tsx (lines 302-308) both import ElementComponentProps and narrowParams<T> from astrid/packs/builtin/elements/_shared/contracts and follow the documented boundary pattern.",
          "The shared contracts.ts comment block (lines 28-38) explicitly states components should declare a Params type and call narrowParams at the top of the render to convert unknown into a real Params value \u2014 this component does neither."
        ],
