    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::unrationalized_type_ignore_return_value_in_tuple_returns": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::unrationalized_type_ignore_return_value_in_tuple_returns",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Several functions silence return-value with `# type: ignore` instead of tightening their return type to a Literal-pair",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/task/plan.py",
          "astrid/core/task/gate.py",
          "astrid/core/adapter/manual.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/core/task/plan.py L278 declares `-> tuple[AssigneeForm, str | None]` (AssigneeForm is Literal[\u2026]), but L283/L291 return `assignee, None` / `kind, ident` with `# type: ignore[return-value]`. The string literals on those lines are already Literal members; the suppression exists only because the local variables `assignee` / `kind` are typed `str`.",
          "astrid/core/task/gate.py L1182 declares `-> tuple[str, str]` (too loose) and then suppresses three returns at L1190/L1198/L1210. Tightening the signature to `tuple[Literal[\"agent\", \"actor\"], str]` would let the literals flow through without ignores.",
          "astrid/core/adapter/manual.py L59 returns `DispatchResult(status=\"dispatched\", started_at=payload[\"dispatched_at\"])  # type: ignore[arg-type]`. `payload` is typed `dict[str, object]` so `payload[\"dispatched_at\"]` is `object`. The suppression hides the fact that the local could be kept as a typed `str` instead of round-tripping through the dict."
        ],
        "suggestion": "plan.py: declare local `assignee: AssigneeForm = \"system\"` (etc.) or use typing.cast at the return, then drop the ignores. gate.py: change the signature to `tuple[Literal[\"agent\", \"actor\"], str]` and drop the three ignores. adapter/manual.py: extract `dispatched_at: str = _utc_now_iso()`, write `payload[\"dispatched_at\"] = dispatched_at`, then `return DispatchResult(status=\"dispatched\", started_at=dispatched_at)` \u2014 no cast, no ignore. None of these add files or abstractions; each is a 1-3 line tightening that removes a suppression.",
