    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::executor_parser_widens_str_to_literal_at_construction": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::executor_parser_widens_str_to_literal_at_construction",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "executor/schema.py parser constructs Literal-typed fields with the str return of _optional_string/_require_string, bypassing the new Literal aliases",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/executor/schema.py",
          "astrid/contracts/schema.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/core/executor/schema.py L241 `kind=data[\"kind\"]` \u2014 `data[\"kind\"]` is `Any`, ExecutorDefinition.kind is `ExecutorKind` (Literal); L265 `type=_optional_string(...)` for ExecutorPort.type which is `PortType` (Literal); L278-279 same for Output.type/mode; L327 `strategy=_require_string(...)` for ExternalRuntimeInstall.strategy (Literal); L365 `kind=_require_string(...)` for ConditionSpec.kind (Literal).",
          "`_require_string` and `_optional_string` both return plain `str`. The dataclass fields are now Literal aliases (good), but construction does the str\u2192Literal widening with no typing.cast and no `# type: ignore`. The follow-on `_validate_executor` step does enforce the value at runtime, but the type system does not see that linkage.",
          "The matching downstream symptom shows up at astrid/core/element/registry.py L73 `kind=kind,  # type: ignore[arg-type]`: the dict key is `str` but ElementConflict.kind is Literal \u2014 same gap, different module."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Add a small `_require_literal(data, key, allowed: frozenset[str], path) -> <Literal>` helper next to `_require_string`/`_optional_string` that validates membership inline and uses `typing.cast` at the return. Use it for the kind / type / mode / strategy fields in both executor/schema.py and (after the orchestrator-schema migration) orchestrator/schema.py. This collapses the parse + validate step for these fields into one place and lets the dataclass construction sites carry the precise Literal type. It also removes the `# type: ignore[arg-type]` in element/registry.py L73 (use `typing.cast(ElementKind, kind)` from the loop key).",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "a07d3e4e"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
      "first_seen": "2026-05-16T08:47:31+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-16T08:47:31+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-05-16T09:59:56+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "agent_import",
        "text": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
        "attested_at": "2026-05-16T09:59:56+00:00",
        "scan_verified": false
      }
    },
    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::root_canvas_inline_structural_type": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::root_canvas_inline_structural_type",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Root.tsx getCanvas defines the theme_overrides shape as an inline structural literal instead of referencing the existing SharedThemeOverrides + canvas types",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "remotion/src/Root.tsx",
          "remotion/src/types.generated.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Root.tsx lines 31-40: `const overrides = (props.timeline.theme_overrides ?? {}) as {visual?: {canvas?: {width?: number; height?: number; fps?: number}}};` \u2014 the canvas shape is invented at the cast site.",
          "types.generated.ts line 212-220 already defines SharedThemeOverrides with `visual?: Record<string, unknown>`, and the canvas object is referenced again as `DEFAULT_CANVAS = {width: 1920, height: 1080, fps: 30}` on line 29 with no shared type.",
          "Upstream @banodoco/timeline-composition/typescript/src/types.ts declares `theme_overrides?: unknown`, which is what forces the cast \u2014 but the cast target is local and could be a named type."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract a `type CanvasSpec = {width: number; height: number; fps: number}` (or `Partial<CanvasSpec>`) in Root.tsx and reuse it for DEFAULT_CANVAS plus the inner cast: `as Pick<SharedThemeOverrides, 'visual'> & {visual?: {canvas?: Partial<CanvasSpec>}}`. That makes the source of the looseness (upstream `unknown`) visible at the seam and removes the duplicated shape literal.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "12bce6d2"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
      "first_seen": "2026-05-16T08:47:31+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-16T08:47:31+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-05-16T09:59:56+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
