    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::executor_schema_mixed_validate_cast_idioms": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::executor_schema_mixed_validate_cast_idioms",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "executor/schema.py uses both _require_literal and _validate_in_allowed+cast for the same validate-then-cast purpose",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/executor/schema.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "_require_literal(data.get(key), ALLOWED, path, LiteralType) is used at 6 construction sites (lines 267, 291, 306, 309, 398, 433) and is the helper added specifically to centralize this pattern.",
          "Four sibling sites (lines 333, 350, 368, 412) for ExternalRuntimeMode, ExternalRuntimeSourceKind, ExternalRuntimeInstallStrategy, and ConditionKind use the older two-step idiom: `_validate_in_allowed(str_val, ALLOWED, path)` followed by `mode: ExternalRuntimeMode = cast(ExternalRuntimeMode, mode_str)` on the next line.",
          "Both shapes are sound at runtime \u2014 the inconsistency is purely a navigability cost in a file whose explicit purpose is to centralize this pattern."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Migrate the four _validate_in_allowed+cast call-sites to _require_literal so the file has one idiom: replace `mode_str = _optional_string(data,'mode',mode_path,default='package'); _validate_in_allowed(mode_str, EXTERNAL_RUNTIME_MODES, mode_path); mode: ExternalRuntimeMode = cast(ExternalRuntimeMode, mode_str)` with `mode = _require_literal(data.get('mode','package'), EXTERNAL_RUNTIME_MODES, mode_path, ExternalRuntimeMode)`. After conversion, _validate_in_allowed may have no remaining callers and can be removed.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "f8525931"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-16T09:59:56+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-16T09:59:56+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::root_tsx_inline_theme_overrides_cast": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::root_tsx_inline_theme_overrides_cast",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "remotion/src/Root.tsx getCanvas casts theme_overrides inline via two `as` chains instead of referencing shared canvas type",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "remotion/src/Root.tsx",
          "remotion/src/types.augmentations.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 36-46 of Root.tsx implement getCanvas by chaining `props.timeline.theme_overrides as TimelineThemeOverrides | undefined` then `overrides?.visual as VisualOverrides | undefined`, ultimately falling back to a separately-declared DEFAULT_CANVAS literal at line 34.",
          "TimelineThemeOverrides, VisualOverrides, and CanvasOverride already exist as imports (lines 8-12); the casts demonstrate the typing system knows the right shape but the runtime value is untrusted at this seam.",
          "DEFAULT_CANVAS at line 34 is declared as `{width: 1920, height: 1080, fps: 30}` with no annotation, parallel to the shape used elsewhere \u2014 a small parallel type definition risk."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Annotate `const DEFAULT_CANVAS: CanvasOverride = {width: 1920, height: 1080, fps: 30};` so the constant participates in the same type as the function's return. The two `as` casts on lines 37 and 40 can stay (they're at the untyped Remotion props seam) but the inner DEFAULT_CANVAS fallback should reference the shared type rather than rely on structural inference.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "4077beaa"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-16T09:59:56+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-16T09:59:56+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
